# The RK-ZYNQ7100's processing_system7 configuration, as a flat property list.
#
# Taken VERBATIM, apart from TTC1 (below), from
# hardware/board-files/ps_reference.tcl in
# github.com/R0Y00/rk-zynq7100-fmcomms2-linux (commit 461efa3), the PS7 block
# of a design that was run on this board: DDR trained, Linux booted, QSPI, eMMC,
# SD, Ethernet and USB all worked. Only the Tcl wrapper differs -- the block
# design's `set_property -dict [list ...] $processing_system7_0` became the
# PS7_CONFIG list below so a non-project script can apply it.
#
# ⚠ Some of it belongs to that repository's FMCOMMS2 design, not to the board:
# SPI0 on EMIO, 64 EMIO GPIOs, S_AXI_HP1/HP2, the fabric interrupt, FCLK1 at
# 200 MHz. None of it touches DDR, MIO or boot, and all of it is harmless with
# no bitstream loaded, so it stays -- a hand-trimmed copy is a copy nobody has
# run. PL builds regenerate boot Tcl from this file automatically; after an
# edit, also refresh the tracked GPL C/H sources using linux/gen_ps7.tcl.
#
# One setting is NOT from that repository: TTC1, enabled with its waveform
# outputs on EMIO. The fan's PWM pin is a PL pin (W21), so a PS timer can only
# reach it through the fabric, and TTC1_WAVE0_OUT is what Linux's pwm-cadence
# driver drives. TTC0 is left alone: the kernel registers it as
# ttc_clocksource.
#
# The PCW_ACT_* entries are values Vivado computes, not settings; gen_ps7.tcl
# skips them.
